## 6. Insights  

- **Top Predictors of Fraud:**  
  - `collision_type` (e.g., “rear collision”)  
  - `property_damage` (Y/N)  
  - `incident_severity` (major vs. minor)  
  - Policyholder injury flags  
  - Vehicle age & witness statements  

- **Threshold Selection Matters:**  
  Lowering cutoff increases recall (catch more fraud) at the expense of precision (more false alarms). An optimal cutoff of ~0.45 balances both, but business metrics (cost of investigation vs. cost of missed fraud) should guide the final choice.

- **Ensemble Gains:**  
  Random forest outperformed logistic regression by ∼3–5 percentage points in F1‑score, thanks to capturing nonlinear interactions and handling mixed feature types without standardization.

